  "courseSlug": "azure-problems",
  "title": "Blob Storage Access Tiers",
  "description": "Optimize Azure Blob Storage costs using Hot, Cool, Cold, and Archive tiers.",
  "order": 1,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "tags": ["azure", "storage", "blob", "access-tiers", "cost"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Problem Statement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "You store 50TB of data in Azure Blob Storage: 30TB active (accessed daily), 15TB infrequent (accessed monthly), and 5TB archival (rarely accessed). Your monthly storage bill is $2,500 but should be $800. How do you optimize?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "What to Do"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use **Blob Storage access tiers**: Hot for active data, Cool for infrequent access, Cold for rare access, and Archive for compliance backups. Implement **lifecycle management policies** to automate tier transitions."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "How to Implement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "ARM Template - Lifecycle Management Policy",
        "language": "json",
        "code": "{\n  \"type\": \"Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/blobServices\",\n  \"apiVersion\": \"2023-01-01\",\n  \"name\": \"[concat(parameters('storageAccountName'), '/default')]\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"containerProperties\": {\n      \"policy\": {\n        \"rules\": [\n          {\n            \"name\": \"MoveToCool\",\n            \"type\": \"Lifecycle\",\n            \"definition\": {\n              \"filters\": {\n                \"blobTypes\": [\"blockBlob\"],\n                \"prefixMatch\": [\"logs/\"]\n              },\n              \"actions\": {\n                \"baseBlob\": {\n                  \"tierToCool\": { \"daysAfterModificationGreaterThan\": 30 }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Azure CLI - Set Blob Tier",
        "language": "bash",
        "code": "# Set blob tier to Archive\naz storage blob set-tier \\\n  --account-name 'mystorage' \\\n  --container-name 'backups' \\\n  --name 'backup-2024.zip' \\\n  --tier Archive \\\n  --auth-mode login"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Why Access Tiers Matter"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Access tiers can reduce storage costs by **50-90%**. Hot tier costs ~$0.018/GB/month. Archive costs ~$0.00099/GB/month. For 50TB, using tiers appropriately saves ~$1,700/month."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "comparison-cards",
      "data": {
        "title": "Blob Access Tiers",
        "cards": [
          {
            "title": "Hot Tier",
            "description": "Frequently accessed data",
            "pros": ["Low retrieval cost", "High availability", "99.9% SLA"],
            "cons": ["Higher storage cost", "No minimum storage duration"],
            "tags": ["Active data", "Recommended"]
          },
          {
            "title": "Cool Tier",
            "description": "Infrequently accessed data (30+ days)",
            "pros": ["Lower storage cost", "High availability", "99.9% SLA"],
            "cons": ["Higher retrieval cost", "30-day minimum"],
            "tags": ["Backups", "Archives"]
          },
          {
            "title": "Archive Tier",
            "description": "Rarely accessed data (180+ days)",
            "pros": ["Lowest storage cost", "Compliance storage"],
            "cons": ["Rehydration time (hours)", "180-day minimum", "Lower availability"],
            "tags": ["Compliance", "Long-term"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
